<!--
  The `secrets` case as a complete Resolved Deployment model, the transformation's
  output reviewed value by value against the specification.

  It is NOT an oracle. `secrets` carries no production `resolved.json`, and its
  dependencies oracle holds no edge, so this file is the one check on the rest of
  its resolution: ResolutionTest holds the transformation's output equal to it.

  Every value is derivable from `spec/v1/examples/secrets/secrets.project.yml`,
  the project files of the foundation it composes with, and the Platform document
  and pinned inputs beside them: a 30s startup budget gives a 90s deadline and six
  startup attempts five seconds apart, an interrupted cutover a stop-start switch
  under a Recreate strategy with a Service rather than a Canary, and every node of
  the contract holds one copy. The Process's network policy admits no peer
  inbound: the derived allow set gives a grant holder egress to the Secret Store
  and the Store no matching ingress (spec/v1/16-dependencies.md#the-derived-allow-set).
  The digests are what the transformation computes, and bind this implementation
  only.
-->
